A||N||5||Bizquik||87 isuzu shifting prob||||4||
Z||000000||Bizquik||12-03-2001||10:10 AM||||I have an 87 2m4 with the isuzu five speed and this morning after starting up my car i couldnt put it in any gear whatsoever! when i turned the car off i then could easily throw it into any gear i chose. so (with the car off) i put it into rev. then started it and it went but i had to turn it off again to get it into first, ugh! what could it be that while the car runs it wont go into gear? i plan to take a look at it all today, but the car is new to me and any help would be much appreciated ||||reg||4
Z||000001||johnt671||12-03-2001||10:44 AM||||The 1st thing I would try is bleeding the system and see if you have air in the slave.  Also make sure that the rod on the slave is pushing out when you depress the clutch.  Did you hear or feel anything funny the last time you drove it?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bizquik||12-03-2001||12:12 PM||||Last time i drove it (last night) the car wouldnt let me put it in 5th gear once on the highway (i was going about 65) so i then tried to put it in to 4th, no can do, so slowing down as i was in nuetral i pulled over to a stop, i cant remember if i turned the car off but i was able to put it into all the gears. got back on the highway and it went through fine, (maybe sticking a bit) Then later off the highway making a turn i couldnt downshift to second (i was down to a good speed of like 15-20) but 3rd worked, it was doing things like sticking in nuetral in between various gears all through the ride home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and like i posted earlier, now nothing works unless the car's off. oh yeah i noticed when i got it moving in reverse this morning there was like no clutch left, like it moved the car without pulling it out a centimeter (and its been used day in day out since i got it a month and a half ago without these probs) hope i described it clear  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||12-03-2001||12:55 PM||||I'm not a clutch xpert but it sound like you have a bad clutch.  Was hoping it was a simple problem..  I would still try bleeding the system and see what happens.  It would eliminate a hydraulic problem with the clutch master cylinder and slave cylinder.   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||tesmith66||12-03-2001||12:57 PM||||You have several things to look at:<P>Look for fluid leaks at the clutch slave cylinder (at the hose fitting and under the boot at the rod end) and at the master cylinder (look for oily residue on the firewall around the master cylinder, and inside the car where the pushrod goues through the firewall).<P>Make sure the master cylinder pushrod is not bent (they bend easily).<P>The clutch pedal could be bent (impossible to tell by looking at it in the car, the best fix is just replace it with a steel one)<P><BR>Also, check my reply at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015463.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015463.html</A> <P>Fieros have crappy clutch systems. Period.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||4
Z||000005||Bizquik||12-03-2001||05:23 PM||||Hey thanks guys, yeah thats quite a chunk of possiblilities, Tim (can i call you Tim), double thx for that info. You wouldnt believe what just happened: we bled the clutch system and it went around the block fine! with plenty more clutch let-off distance (clutch not as worn as i thought). man, i get real lucky sometimes! coulda been an expensive job (not to say that come spring time i wont replace those other potential problem-parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) Thanks again guys!||||reg||1
